>> title: Croissant
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: pastry, laminated, breakfast, butter, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: croissant, croissants, butter croissant, croissant au beurre, plain croissant, crescent roll
>> pairs-with: croissant-dough, almond-croissant
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: narrow — the proof is judged by a wobble: under-proofed they push their butter out into the pan, over-proofed they collapse as they bake

>> step: roll to a 8x24-in sheet
Roll @croissant dough{1%batch}(cold, one batch of croissant-dough) out on @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(for dusting) to a sheet 8 inches deep and 24 inches long, a scant quarter-inch thick.

>> step: cut twelve triangles and roll each one up
Cut @&(~1)dough sheet{} into twelve triangles with a 4-inch base, stretch each by its point, and roll it up from the base — three turns showing, point underneath.

>> step: proof 2 hr, until they wobble
Proof @&(~1)shaped croissants{} on lined trays at room temperature for ~proof{2%hr}, until they have nearly doubled and wobble as one piece when the tray is shaken.

>> step: beat the egg wash
Beat @egg{1%large} with @whole milk{1%Tbs}(15 mL) until it is loose enough to brush without dragging.

>> step: brush and bake 400°F (205°C) 18 min
Brush @&(~2)proofed croissants{} with @&(~1)egg wash{} and bake in a 400°F (205°C) #oven{} for ~bake{18%min}, until they are deep brown at the ridges and sound hollow.
